# PulseUp Fitness Website

A multi-page fitness website prototype combining a promotional landing page with account, dashboard, goals, and statistics screens. The project demonstrates a responsive front end built with standard web technologies and browser-side interactions.

## Core features

- Multi-page experience for home, about, contact, sign-up, dashboard, goals, and statistics.
- Shared styling and navigation across the site.
- Client-side form and account interactions implemented in JavaScript.
- Fitness-oriented content, progress views, and promotional media references.

## Technology

HTML5 - 
CSS3 - 
JavaScript

## Architecture and data flow

There is no server-side application or database in the supplied source. Account-related state is handled in the browser, so the site is a front-end demonstration rather than a production authentication system.

## Requirements

- A modern web browser
- Python 3 for the optional local static server

## Installation and usage

From PowerShell, enter the folder containing `index.html` and start a local server:


Open [http://localhost:8000](http://localhost:8000) in your browser. Stop the server with `Ctrl+C`.

## Roadmap

- Improve responsive and accessibility behavior across all pages.
- Replace browser-only account handling with a properly secured service before any real user sign-in.
- Add form validation and automated browser tests.
- Document permitted image/video assets and provide optimized alternatives.

